# __FH_MODULE__

Complete fh application starter with secure defaults.

## Run

```sh
cp .env.example .env
go mod tidy
go run ./cmd/server
```

The starter includes `fh` secure-by-default middleware, signed sessions,
database access through `squealx`, `config` secret loading, structured `zlog`,
file-backed RBAC through `authz`, SPL server-rendered templates, and the
secure WASM fetch integration. Replace the development credentials and secret
values before deployment.

Use `make check` for the application checks and `make wasm` to build the
secure-fetch client after installing Node.js and TypeScript.
